Task 4
  Explain with your own example the difference between entry-controlled and exit-controlled loops by writing a short code snippet for each (for/while vs do-while)
    and describing what happens if the loop condition is false at the start.
Answer
#include<stdio.h>
int main()
{
	int i=5;
	printf("while loop \nEnter control\nIt chek condition first\n");
	while(i>=10)
	{
		printf("%d",i);
	}
	printf("it does't execute because conditon is false\n\n\n");
	printf("do while loop\nexit control\nit execute 1 time and then chek condition\n");
	do
	{
		printf("code run 1 time");
	}while(i>=10);
}
